Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] arm64: dts: komodo: enable the Synaptics S3908 touchscreen

Enable the touchscreen node that the board DTS already describes. The
stock komodo DTBO (board_id 0x60806, rev 0x10000) puts a Synaptics
TouchComm controller ("synaptics,tcm-spi", firmware suffix S3908TG) on
spi_20 = spi@111d0000, with ATTN on gpn0-0 (level low), reset on gpp1-1
(active low), AVDD = S2MPG14 LDO4M 3.3 V and VDD = S2MPG14 LDO25M 1.8 V,
SPI mode 0 at 10 MHz: the same wiring as this node. The in-tree
synaptics_tcm driver (CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_SYNAPTICS_TCM_SPI=y) needs no
firmware file: the controller runs the application firmware in its own
flash.

Not tested on this exact tree. Upstream PR #276 left the node disabled
by policy ("optional ... nodes remain disabled"); its author enabled it
with a one-line DT overlay on a local integration build and saw
"Synaptics TouchComm Touchscreen" report BTN_TOUCH and ABS events.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
@@ -2,8 +2,8 @@
 /*
  * Google Pixel 9 Pro XL (komodo) board identification.
  *
- * Boot, storage, display and USB2 paths are described here. Experimental
- * touch, Type-C, WLAN and GPU devices remain disabled.
+ * Boot, storage, display, USB2 and touch paths are described here.
+ * Experimental Type-C, WLAN and GPU devices remain disabled.
  */
 
 /dts-v1/;
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-/* ACPM owns the PMIC rails used by the USB2 PHY and the disabled touch node. */
+/* ACPM owns the PMIC rails used by the USB2 PHY and the touchscreen. */
 &acpm_ipc {
 	status = "okay";
 
@@ -402,7 +402,6 @@
 		reset-gpios = <&gpp1 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		avdd-supply = <&touch_avdd>;
 		vdd-supply = <&touch_vdd>;
-		status = "disabled";
 	};
 };
 
